 "verdict": "Frame counter, not odometer. Zero-speed twins (disk centroid constant to 6e-14 px) still advance along V-JEPA 2's time code at 0.55-1.07 of the moving rate (point 12: mean direction 1.07 [1.05, 1.08], spline coordinate 0.55 [0.52, 0.59], mid-band probe 0.65 [0.64, 0.66]; point 22: 0.69, 0.83, 0.52), never near the odometer's 0; the untrained copy advances at the frame rate (1.02-1.10, CIs include 1). V-JEPA 2's static per-step spline coordinate follows the frame counter exactly at steps 0-4 and 6 and falls back to ~3 at steps 5 and 7 (the step-centroid curve folds back on itself, 5-6x longer than end to end, so the nearest-point projection is ambiguous there), which is what pulls the spline and probe slopes below 1. Static clips are off the moving-clip manifold: nearest-neighbour distance 2.3x (point 12) and 2.9x (point 22) that of the moving twins, and only 0.45 / 0.56 of their within-clip variance lies on the shared curve (moving 0.79 / 0.80)."
